Lepton: VA-API direct output (the GPU converts into Android's buffer)

With debug.ffmpeg-codec2.hwaccel.drm=true and
debug.ffmpeg-codec2.pixel_format=YUV_420_PLANER (upstream's "VPP mode"),
FFmpeg decodes into its own VA surfaces and the GPU's video processor
converts each frame into the Android YV12 buffer, imported as a VA
surface. No readback, no CPU conversion. The launcher selects this by
default when hardware decoding is on (LEPTON_VIDEO_HWACCEL_OUTPUT=direct).

Fixes to upstream's VPP mode:
- no 64-alignment of the advertised picture size; the buffer is aligned,
  the conversion covers the picture only and the output is cropped to it;
- same matrix in and out (as copy-back), from the frame's tags, both sides
  declared full range so that no driver remaps values (Mesa 26.0's VA
  post-processing otherwise squeezes limited range a second time);
- wait for the decode before the conversion and for the conversion before
  the buffer reaches the framework; keep the decoded surface until then;
- request the same buffers as copy-back (CPU-mappable YV12): minigbm
  refuses YV12 for decoder-only usage;
- describe Android's YV12 as I420 with the U plane first: Mesa writes a
  YV12 import's chroma in I420 order;
- drop the imports of ByteBuffer-mode buffers (no BufferQueue slot) when
  their frame is released, so they do not keep every buffer alive;
- read minigbm handle fields only after the size check of patch 0021;
- any failure (no video processor, import refused, GPU error), and
  interlaced frames, switch the session to copy-back
  (LEPTON_VA_DIRECT fallback=...); the failed frame's buffer is released.

Diagnostics: LEPTON_VA_SESSION output=, LEPTON_VA_DIRECT,
LEPTON_VA_DIRECT_END (copyback_frames=0 means no CPU readback),
LEPTON_VA_SLOW, LEPTON_VA_PERCENTILES and LEPTON_VA_DEADLINE (process()
includes waits for the app's output queue, so long calls are not dropped
frames).
Test switch: debug.ffmpeg-codec2.direct-validation=pixels compares two
output buffers per session with the decoded surface
(LEPTON_VA_DIRECT_PIXELS); =fallback fails the fourth frame to exercise
the fallback.

